-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/55e1ee8c-7b1f-57b3-87c1-8badbe7f0191
-- title:
--   Pro-étale pullbacks of étale sheaves send cofiltered limits of affine étale schemes to colimits
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a scheme and $\mathcal A$ a coefficient category with small colimits and limits, exact filtered colimits (AB5), weak sheafification for the pro-étale and affine pro-étale topologies, and such that pushforward of sheaves from the pro-étale site has a left adjoint. Write $\nu^*$ for the pullback of sheaves from the small étale site to the small pro-étale site of $S$. A functor $P : \mathcal D^{\mathrm{op}} \to \mathcal A$ is said to **preserve relative filtered colimits** along $F : \mathcal C \to \mathcal D$ if for every small cofiltered diagram $K$ in $\mathcal C$ and every limit cone $c$ of $F \circ K$ in $\mathcal D$, $P$ sends $c$ to a colimit cocone.
--
--   This file contains:
--   1. This property of $P$ is invariant under isomorphism of functors $P \cong Q$.
--   2. For every sheaf $F$ on the small étale site of $S$ with values in $\mathcal A$, the restriction of $\nu^*F$ to the small affine pro-étale site preserves relative filtered colimits along the inclusion of the affine étale site into the affine pro-étale site: for $U = \lim_i U_i$ a cofiltered limit of affine étale $S$-schemes (computed in the affine pro-étale site),
--   $$(\nu^*F)(U) = \operatorname*{colim}_i F(U_i).$$
--   This is Bhatt–Scholze, Lemma 5.1.1, obtained by transporting the corresponding property of the left Kan extension along the canonical isomorphism with the sheaf pullback.
--
--   This instance is the input for Bhatt–Scholze, Lemma 5.1.2 (the module documentation describes that lemma: $\nu^*$ is fully faithful, and its essential image — the *classical* sheaves — consists of the sheaves $G$ with $G(U) = \operatorname{colim}_i G(U_i)$ for every affine pro-étale $U = \lim_i U_i$), whose proofs are not part of this file.
--
--   **Formalization Note** For `S : Scheme.{u}`, coefficients `A` with `HasColimitsOfSize.{u, u + 1}`, `HasFilteredColimitsOfSize.{u, u}`, `AB5OfSize.{u, u}`, `HasLimitsOfSize.{u, u + 1}`, `HasWeakSheafify` for `ProEt.topology S` and `AffineProEt.topology S`, and `(ProEt.sheafPushforward S A).IsRightAdjoint`. The declarations are `CategoryTheory.Functor.PreservesRelativeFilteredColimits.of_iso` and the instance `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.preservesRelativeFilteredColimits_sheafPullback`, stated for the functor `(AffineProEt.toProEt S).op ⋙ ((sheafPullback S A).obj F).obj` along `AffineEtale.toAffineProEt S`, with index categories in universe `u`. The results named in the module docstring (`fullyFaithfulSheafPullback`, `mem_essImage_sheafPullback_iff`, etc.) are not contained in this definitions file.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014); cited in the code: Bhatt–Scholze, Lemma 5.1.1; Bhatt–Scholze, Lemma 5.1.2. Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Topology/Comparison/Classical.lean (declarations needed by the transplanted proofs, unused ones removed).

